<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48046" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῖον</span></b>  (A), 
			Ep.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέειον</span></b>  (in <i><span class="en">
			Od.
			22.493
		</span></i>
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θήϊον</span></b> ), τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>brimstone</i>,
			used to fumigate and purify, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέπας . . ἐκάθηρε θεείῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.228
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶσε θέειον . . , κακῶν ἄκος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					22.481
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεινὴ δὲ θεείου γίγνεται
			ὀδμή</span>, from a thunderbolt, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				14.415
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν δὲ θεείου πλῆτο</span>, of
			a ship struck by lightning, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				12.417
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμβαλόντες πῦρ ξὺν θ</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.77
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				4.100
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κύριος ἔβρεξεν ἐπὶ Σόδομα καὶ
					Γόμορρα θ. καὶ πῦρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Ge.</u>
					19.24
				</span></i>
			; as a natural product, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i><i>Aër.</i><i><span class="en">
				7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.21
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				143
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ti.Locr.
				99c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. ἄπυρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					12.903
				</span></i>
			; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεπυρωμένον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				5.107
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεάφιον, θέαφος</span>.
			(Perh. cogn. with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύω, θυμιάω</span>,
			Lat. <i>suffire.</i>)</div>
